{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_dbec72dc32e668aa0e9e79d3d9a21398f7382454419c5fba6d3ad30f86ea5ebd", "title": "Varaprasad Rao Velagapalli", "text": "Varaprasad Rao Velagapalli is an Indian politician and a member of parliament to the 16th Lok Sabha from Tirupati (Lok Sabha constituency), Andhra Pradesh. He won the Indian general election, 2014 being a Yuvajana Sramika Rythu Congress Party candidate.", "score": 69.5431}, {"id": "hp_doc_6b22c6a3ab1e7f8fc801c279e4a9fa0c60aaa0ec4bd3cb5dd2710e8fd084814e", "title": "Campaigning in the Indian general election, 2014", "text": "The Indian general election of 2014 were held to constitute the 16th Lok Sabha in India. Voting took place in all 543 parliamentary constituencies of India to elect members of parliament in the Lok Sabha. The result of this election was declared on 16 May. The 15th Lok Sabha completed its constitutional mandate on 31 May 2014.", "score": 35.3431}, {"id": "hp_doc_00ec3c8a54f468be78cf73c548f98fda390a0a190e8e5005f2dd9d8b39b21b35", "title": "Brij Bhushan Sharan Singh", "text": "Brij Bhushan Sharan Singh (born 8 January 1957) is an Indian politician. In 1991, he was elected to the 10th Lok Sabha from Gonda constituency in Uttar Pradesh state (India) as a Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) candidate. He was re-elected to the 13th Lok Sabha in 1999 from the same constituency and in 2004, he was re-elected to 14th Lok Sabha from Balrampur constituency in Uttar Pradesh state on the BJP ticket. On 20 July 2008, he joined the Samajwadi Party. In 2009, he was re-elected to 15th Lok Sabha from Kaiserganj constituency in Uttar Pradesh state. He later joined the Bharatiya Janata Party months before the 16th general election and is currently member of 16th Lok Sabha from BJP He is the President of Wrestling Federation of India(WFI).", "score": 30.5788}], "remaining_searches": 2}
